ash":"732c8f8c84bf45296bba078123f2d186c8846802a8923bd6efae9b1d5b778968","event_uuid":"48829f95-861b-44e8-8027-df4bf30ac160","position":{"commit_sha":"e8fefa1be52944cfd72733ff6eec1da844bde3e7","position":"1793813843440298001-48829f95-861b-44e8-8027-df4bf30ac160"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-308_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Recurrence 2026-11-04 PST: make verify on worktree fix-jaeger (commit d413a0497e5, bug bronze-commonable-jaeger, which touches only MCP auth wiring) failed only this test with the same TimeoutError at tests/unit/test_audit_serve.py:292: 1 failed, 20749 passed, 27 skipped, default tier wall 3:01:25 (documented norm 22-26 min). Host load average was 33 on 18 cores right after. Isolated reruns: 5/5 pass on the branch (5.0-7.7 s each) and 3/3 pass on origin/main. Consistent with the load hypothesis in this ticket; not reproduced deterministically here.","timestamp":1793797012731825001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause (TEST bug), measured: the index render runs the store read path (first-read freshness fetch + one `git rev-parse` probe per read, `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:221`), about 6 git child processes for one audited ticket, 0.2-0.45 s unloaded. Deterministic repro: PATH shim git sleeping 0.8 s per call -> unchanged test fails with the same `TimeoutError` (1 failed, 68 s); 0 s -> passes.\nFix (tests/unit/test_audit_serve.py only): state-based readiness wait (started or thread exited), bind assertion on the listening socket, no client read deadline (hang -> suite pytest-timeout 300 s), companion occupied-port test.\nAfter: slow-git 0.8 s and 1.5 s shims -> passes (23 s / 41 s call). Mutants: readiness wait ignoring thread death -> companion hits the per-test timeout; binding 0.0.0.0 -> bind assertion fails. 11 audit modules 76 passed; make lint and make typecheck exit 0.\nDiscovered: synonymous-destined-cricket (probe-before-throttle git spawn). Gerrit change 3305.","timestamp":1793805588625119001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit 3305: LLM-Review +1. Verified -1 twice, both environmental: run 41856506741's pytest (macos-latest, py3.13) was CANCELLED with GitHub's annotation 'The job was not acquired by Runner of type hosted even after multiple attempts' (no log; all other cells, including ubuntu py3.13 default + integration tiers, passed). Recheck run 41861026778 drew Verified -1 at 08:18 PST while GitHub's API still shows its macOS cell queued with no runner and every step of the other cells green. Changes 3304 and 3307 failed identically in the same window; githubstatus.com reports an unresolved 'Incident with Actions and Pages'. Waiting for the incident to clear before one more recheck.","timestamp":1793809204211741001}],"created_at":1793776034975850001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e8e41b1f-c697-4d58-9ff9-3fba538fea06","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ad14-c714-4619-4cd2"},{"link_uuid":"c8ff26f9-4824-4c18-80a5-847fe1ffab0e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"47a0-c680-eb6a-4551"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`tests/unit/test_audit_serve.py::test_serve_binds_loopback_ephemeral_and_lists_ticket` fails with `TimeoutError: timed out` on its `urllib.request.urlopen(..., timeout=5)` during loaded full `make verify` runs (fix-chihuahua at 4f8cd749a61; fix-jaeger at d413a0497e5, load average 33 on 18 cores), while passing in isolation (5/5 on the branch, 3/3 on origin/main). Closed bug ignitable-noteworthy-osprey was a different failure (network guard leak), so this is a separate cause.\n\n## Root cause (measured)\nThe 5 s read bound covers the whole `GET /` render, and that render spawns git child processes whose cost scales with host load, not with the HTTP contract:\n- `create_app`'s index (`src/rebar/audit/server.py` `_audited_tickets`) calls `rebar.list_tickets` then `audit_trail` per ticket (`src/rebar/audit/read.py:205-217`).\n- Every one of those reads runs `ensure_fresh` (`src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:192`), which spawns `git rev-parse --verify <branch>` at line 221 before the 60 s marker throttle, and on the first read a `git fetch` via `_store/sync.py` `_coordinated_fetch`.\n- Profiled with one audited ticket: 6 git processes on the first render (fetch + 5 rev-parse), 5 on a throttled render; 0.2-0.45 s unloaded.\n- Deterministic reproduction: a PATH shim `git` that sleeps 0.8 s before exec'ing the real git makes the unchanged test fail with the same `TimeoutError` every run (1 failed in 68 s); with 0 s delay it passes.\nClassification: TEST bug. The work in the request is the store's uniform read policy, so the test's tight wall-clock bound measures host subprocess cost. The suite's designated hang guard is pytest-timeout (`pyproject.toml` `timeout = 300`, `timeout_method = \"thread\"`, documented as sized to dwarf legitimate cost). The 10 s `uv.started` deadline has the same flaw for server startup. Precedent: Gerrit 3297 (30f06afc412) replaced a wall-clock bound with an ordering check plus a mutant check.\nThe probe-before-throttle cost at `reads.py:221` (1 + 4N git spawns per index render even when throttled) is a real but separate production inefficiency; it is filed as its own bug linked discovered_from this one and is out of scope here.\n\n## Approach\nMake the test measure the contract (binds 127.0.0.1 on the requested ephemeral port, answers 200, lists the seeded ticket) instead of elapsed time:\n1. Readiness by state, not deadline: a helper waits until `uv.started` is true or the server thread has exited. uvicorn 0.52.1 calls `sys.exit(STARTUP_FAILURE)` on a bind `OSError` (`uvicorn/server.py:183`), which ends the thread before `started` is set (`server.py:196`), so a bind failure is reported at once with no deadline.\n2. Assert the bind directly from the listening sockets (`uv.servers[*].sockets[*].getsockname()` == `(\"127.0.0.1\", port)`).\n3. Issue the request with no client-side read deadline; a genuine hang is bounded by the suite's 300 s pytest-timeout budget, the documented hang guard.\n4. Companion mutant check (precedent 3297 style): start the server on a port already held by another socket and assert the readiness helper reports \"thread exited without starting\" promptly instead of waiting, proving the state-based wait still catches the real failure.\nNo production code changes; no autouse fixtures added; no new child processes (if any are needed they go through `tests/_subprocess_env.subprocess_env`).\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_audit_serve.py` — readiness helper, bind assertion, unbounded read, companion bind-failure test.\n\n## Testing\n- Failing first: under the slow-git PATH shim (0.8 s per git call) the current test fails with `TimeoutError`; after the change the same command passes.\n- Companion test: a pre-bound port makes the readiness helper return \"not started\" with the thread dead.\n- Unloaded: `pytest -n0 tests/unit/test_audit_serve.py` passes; `tests/unit -k audit` passes.\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass with the worktree `.venv/bin` first on PATH.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] [non-codebase] Root cause identified with a deterministic reproduction (for example a throttled server thread) before any fix.\n  provenance: environment=local developer host, worktree fix-sealion at 1cb7ea41f0c; principal=Rebar Bot Nava agent session a85e3cd3; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=simulation — a PATH shim git that sleeps 0.8 s before each call made the unchanged test fail with TimeoutError on every run (1 failed in 68 s) and pass at 0 s; per-render git spawn counts and stacks were profiled before any edit; results recorded in this ticket's comments.\n- [x] [non-codebase] The test passes under that reproduction.\n  provenance: environment=local developer host, worktree fix-sealion at commit 1f8380e14fd (merged as b7c6ed6c834, Gerrit 3305); principal=Rebar Bot Nava agent session a85e3cd3; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=simulation — with the same shim at 0.8 s and 1.5 s per git call the changed test passed (23 s and 41 s call time); recorded in this ticket's comments.\n- [x] `test_serve_binds_loopback_ephemeral_and_lists_ticket` contains no wall-clock deadline on server startup or on the HTTP read; it asserts the listening socket is `127.0.0.1:<port>`.\n- [x] A companion test starts the server on an occupied port and asserts the readiness helper reports failure with the server thread exited; it passes.\n- [x] `pytest -n0 tests/unit/test_audit_serve.py` and `pytest tests/unit -k audit` pass; `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit 0.\n- [x] [non-codebase] The probe-before-throttle inefficiency is filed as a bug linked discovered_from this ticket.\n  provenance: environment=shared rebar tickets store (origin tickets branch); principal=Rebar Bot Nava agent session a85e3cd3; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — filed as bug synonymous-destined-cricket (40c3-d22a-3872-4c8c) and linked discovered_from smalltime-repressive-sealion through the rebar CLI on 2026-11-04 PST.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_audit_serve.py","reason":"replace wall-clock startup/read bounds with state-based readiness, bind assertion, and a bind-failure companion test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","47a0-c680-eb6a-4551"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"46bc18e4-f026-4c1e-ac60-e579be60c826","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b0f0-3dd2-fcf2-4707","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_serve_binds_loopback_ephemeral_and_lists_ticket times out its 5 s HTTP read under a loaded full suite","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["cbef7513-4444-4650-be8c-27bdd705b630","58ee17fc-3ad7-4bde-a612-c85d9ab1aba1","0d099d19-effc-4537-bc2a-49ea6417090e","c4e6f72c-5275-400d-ac09-01728e3cf417","46bc18e4-f026-4c1e-ac60-e579be60c826","2132c459-3c23-4212-b666-73d53a8984f6","d595c8ab-3c4e-470c-83a1-3508ae92aace","c8ff26f9-4824-4c18-80a5-847fe1ffab0e","a6ceda66-e8ac-4f04-8105-fe979993b8a3","9d342e31-17b0-4a74-bbd7-49f15521f425","48829f95-861b-44e8-8027-df4bf30ac160"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793813843440298002,"uuid":"8e2c2f10-8492-45e4-b8e4-0a8fcf27d58a"}